From 2bc25e3f444d3079576c34dcc396d7e6042ff23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 23:45:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Bound the desktop driver readiness wait.

load_desktop_driver() sends WM_NULL to the desktop window as a barrier,
so that the display device GUID property is only read once the desktop
thread has finished initializing its driver. The send is unbounded: if
the desktop thread stalls, for example because it is itself blocked
inside driver initialization, every process that goes on to load the
display driver hangs in that barrier forever, without any diagnostic.

Use send_message_timeout() with SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG and a five second
timeout instead, and warn when it expires. The barrier only orders the
property lookup after driver initialization; when it times out the
existing lookup still decides whether a driver is available, and the
caller falls back to the null driver as it already does when the
property is missing.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Schiffhauer <alexander.schiffhauer@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/driver.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/driver.c b/dlls/win32u/driver.c
index a1493750dfa..b3c6c13dba5 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/driver.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/driver.c
@@ -968,8 +968,10 @@ static BOOL load_desktop_driver( HWND hwnd )
     user_check_not_lock();
 
     asciiz_to_unicode( driver_load_error, "The explorer process failed to start." );  /* default error */
-    /* wait for graphics driver to be ready */
-    send_message( hwnd, WM_NULL, 0, 0 );
+    /* wait for graphics driver to be ready, without hanging forever on a stalled desktop thread */
+    send_message_timeout( hwnd, WM_NULL, 0, 0, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 5000, FALSE );
+    if (RtlGetLastWin32Error() == ERROR_TIMEOUT)
+        WARN( "desktop driver readiness wait timed out for %p\n", hwnd );
 
     guid_atom = HandleToULong( NtUserGetProp( hwnd, prop_nameW ));
     memcpy( key, guid_key_prefixW, sizeof(guid_key_prefixW) );
